  "report_period": "Week 45 (3rd Nov to 10th Nov 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Lavinia Corp have committed their Panamax \"Lambay\" & \"Nestor\" 75/2011 Penglai, China (SS/DD 03/2026 & SS 09/2026, DD 03/2026 respectively, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for mid USD 16 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Hong Cheng\" 75/2011 Penglai, China (SS 10/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at USD 17,2 mill. The Ultramax \"Lowlands Mimosa\" 64/2018 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 09/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) of Fukujin Kisen was committed for USD 25,5 mill. The discount in price is due to the fire damage caused in June of 2022. Remind you that the sister vessel \"KK Progression\" 64/2018 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 09/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold back in June at mid USD 28 mill. On the Supramax sector, Chinese owners sold their \"Seacon Dalian\" 57/2010 Cosco, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Indonesian buyers Cakra Buana for USD 12 mill. For comparison, the \"Rhine Confidante\" 57/2010 Ningbo, China (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 10,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"Nippon Maru\" 55/2011 Mitsui, Japan (SS 10/2025, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) of Hayama Senpaku was sold to Greek interests at USD 17,3 mill. Remind you that back in August, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Pythagoras\" 56/2012 Mitsui, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 18,2 mill. In addition, Star Bulk Carriers committed their \"Star Theta\" 52/2003 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 06/2028, DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) for USD 8,5 mill, while the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Bulk Trident\" 52/2005 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 01/2026, DD 04/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 9,8 mill. Dalomar Shipping have sold their Handysize \"Ria\" 34/2012 Dae Sun, Korea (SS 03/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 14,2 mill. Note that a week ago, the \"Darya Jamuna\" 36/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 05/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 16 mill. Moreover, the \"African Ibis\" 32/2004 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted, OHBS) from MUR Shipping was committed at USD 8,6 mill. Remind you that back in October, the \"Sun Ruby\" 32/2004 Kanda, Japan (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,1 mill. Additionally, the \"Lake Dany\" 28/2008 Shimanami, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Greek interests at USD 9 mill basis prompt delivery in China, whilst the \"Valor SW\" 29/2008 Shikoku, Japan (SS 12/2027, DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 8,45 mill.",
    "tankers": "Chemikalien Seetransport have committed their MR1 \"Chemtrans Leo\", \"Chemtrans Mercury\" & \"Chemtrans Uranus\" 37/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 08/2026, DD 11/2024 & SS 03/2026, DD 08/2024 & SS 04/2026, DD 07/2024 respectively, Ice Class 1A) to UAE based buyers for USD 54 mill enbloc. For reference, the \"Baltic Mariner I\" 37/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1B) was sold a month ago at USD 18,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 9,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. A number of Indonesia trips into India were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Continental trips via North Coast South America into Japan were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,500/17,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 550K/750K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 13,000 pd basis delivery China for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into South East Asia were reported fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips into East Coast Mexico were reported at the level of usd 22,000/25,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of East Coast South American trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into India were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
